{"idea_id": "idea_muon_momentum_continuity", "version": 1, "summary": "A verified structural bug (confirmed by 2 agents + git history): the Muon momentum warmup is step-anchored while the warmdown is progress-anchored, causing a +0.063 discontinuity at ~step110 and leaving peak momentum never held. Re-anchoring the warmup to progress is a free, schedule-only fix in the highest-LR window. Likely a non-inferiority baseline correction that also future-proofs throughput levers (which would worsen the step-anchored truncation).", "experimental_plan": "Paired A/B on one seed. Control = baseline (MUON_MOMENTUM_CONTINUOUS=0, buggy step-anchored warmup). Treatment = MUON_MOMENTUM_CONTINUOUS=1 (progress-anchored, continuous). Same frame budget & data order. Read endpoint val_bpb; adopt if improved or non-inferior.", "direction": "optimizer", "subsystem": "muon_momentum", "parent_idea_ids": [], "scores": {"interestingness": {"score": 7, "rationale": "A genuine, non-obvious bug in a well-tuned baseline that survived many commits; free to fix and a dependency for future throughput measurements."}, "novelty": {"score": 6, "rationale": "The bug and fix are specific to this codebase's schedule; not a generic knob and not in the archive."}, "feasibility": {"score": 9, "rationale": "Two-line, schedule-only, zero compute/VRAM change, byte-identical when off."}}, "novelty_check": {"provider": "combined", "status": "passed", "query_rounds": [{"query": "Muon momentum warmup schedule anchoring discontinuity training", "result_paper_ids": ["pap_demon"], "assessment": "Demon establishes momentum-scheduling matters for final performance; no archived idea addresses this codebase's step-vs-progress anchor bug."}], "closest_paper_ids": ["pap_demon"], "evidence_ids": ["evd_lit_demon"], "max_semantic_similarity": 0.35, "discard_threshold": 0.6, "assessment": "Grounded in the Demon momentum-scheduling evidence as the closest prior; the specific step-vs-progress anchor discontinuity is a codebase bug, not in the archive. Distinct subsystem (muon_momentum). Similarity 0.35<0.6."}, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_muon_momentum_continuity", "title": "Fix the Muon momentum schedule discontinuity", "status": "selected", "created_at": "2026-07-25T13:15:00-07:00", "notes": "Round-1 of the reopened campaign; verified structural bug, non-inferiority adoption per Fable review. Non-n-gram, optimizer direction.", "fingerprint": "2cf669b40e0a8287"}
{"idea_id": "idea_rho1_focal_walltime", "version": 1, "summary": "The repo has a dormant RHO1_GAMMA focal-loss knob (w=ce**gamma). Rho-1 shows token-selective loss improves data efficiency; in this underfit 2000-step regime, concentrating gradient on high-loss tokens could raise learning-per-step at negligible wall-time. Risk: self-referential focal (no reference model) may upweight noise.", "experimental_plan": "Paired A/B on one seed. Control = RHO1_GAMMA=0. Treatment = RHO1_GAMMA=0.2. Same budget & data order. Read endpoint val_bpb; if it clears the floor, sweep gamma {0.1,0.3}.", "direction": "data_order", "subsystem": "rho1_focal", "parent_idea_ids": [], "scores": {"interestingness": {"score": 5, "rationale": "A dormant literature-backed knob targeting the underfit regime's informative-token bottleneck; genuinely uncertain."}, "novelty": {"score": 4, "rationale": "Env knob exists but never run; the self-referential focal form differs from Rho-1's reference-model selection."}, "feasibility": {"score": 9, "rationale": "One existing env var, negligible compute, no code change."}}, "novelty_check": {"provider": "combined", "status": "passed", "query_rounds": [{"query": "focal loss token reweighting selective language modeling data efficiency rho-1", "result_paper_ids": ["pap_r2_data_rho1_selective_lm"], "assessment": "Grounded in Rho-1; no archived idea runs RHO1_GAMMA. Distinct subsystem (rho1_focal)."}], "closest_paper_ids": ["pap_r2_data_rho1_selective_lm"], "evidence_ids": ["evd_lit_rho1_focal"], "max_semantic_similarity": 0.4, "discard_threshold": 0.6, "assessment": "Grounded in the Rho-1 selective-LM evidence; the self-referential focal form is distinct and untested here. Similarity 0.4<0.6. Distinct subsystem from momentum/n-gram/throughput."}, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_rho1_focal_walltime", "title": "Focal loss reweighting (Rho-1-inspired)", "status": "selected", "created_at": "2026-07-25T13:30:00-07:00", "notes": "Parallel round (GPUs 2,3) with the momentum fi