{"idea_id": "idea_ve_eps", "version": 1, "summary": "The n-gram VE RMSProp groups use eps=1e-10, so a rarely-hit row's first updates get a near-1/sqrt(v) explosion. A larger eps of 1e-8 damps first-touch overshoot for rare n-grams for steadier rare-token learning per step. Step-neutral.", "experimental_plan": "Paired A/B, one seed; env knob vs baseline; read endpoint val_bpb.", "direction": "memory_retrieval", "subsystem": "ve_eps", "parent_idea_ids": [], "scores": {"interestingness": {"score": 4, "rationale": "tail knob per paper_001"}, "novelty": {"score": 3, "rationale": "env knob, untested in frame B"}, "feasibility": {"score": 9, "rationale": "one env var, coded"}}, "novelty_check": {"provider": "combined", "status": "passed", "query_rounds": [{"query": "ve_eps", "result_paper_ids": ["pap_recent_optim_galore"], "assessment": "loosely grounded in pap_recent_optim_galore; a knob, not a novel algorithm; untested in frame B"}], "closest_paper_ids": ["pap_recent_optim_galore"], "evidence_ids": ["evd_lit_ngram_sparse_grad_throughput"], "max_semantic_similarity": 0.35, "discard_threshold": 0.6, "assessment": "Env knob for memory_retrieval; evidence evd_lit_ngram_sparse_grad_throughput loosely related (honest: low-EV tail lever). Distinct subsystem ve_eps."}, "hypothesis_id": "hyp_ve_eps", "title": "Larger n-gram VE RMSProp eps (1e-10 to 1e-8)", "status": "selected", "created_at": "2026-07-26T05:30:00-07:00", "notes": "batch tail lever, coded in train.py 1fa4d7e8; for GPU occupation per operator directive.", "fingerprint": "c009604969968a7c"}
